publican, against Democrat Annie Andrews, who has dramatically out-raised the incumbent with more than $10 million. The state's eight-point Republican lean and Graham's incumbency give her a structural edge, and outside groups have spent heavily to support her while Andrews has drawn little outside help.\n\nYet recent polls show a surprisingly close contest, with averages placing Graham ahead by only two to four points, and several forecasters have shifted their ratings toward the Democrats in recent days. Prediction markets remain skeptical of an upset, pricing Andrews around 14 to 16 percent. The race sits between those signals: Graham is favored, but the final weeks of debates and advertising could tighten it further.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1565, "margin": -5.15}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2122, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2115, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2143, "margin": -5.0}]}